Pearson distribution sampling (`src/rdspd_atheia/randnonnormal/`)
---------------------------------------------------------------

This module is our own implementation of published, non-proprietary mathematics.
It is not a copy of any third-party package. The algorithms it implements are:

* **The Pearson distribution system** and its classification from the first four
  moments — K. Pearson, "Contributions to the Mathematical Theory of Evolution II"
  (1895); N. L. Johnson, S. Kotz & N. Balakrishnan, *Continuous Univariate
  Distributions*, vol. 1, 2nd ed., ch. 12.

* **Sampling from the Pearson type IV distribution**, including the normalising
  constant expressed through |Γ(m + iν/2) / Γ(m)|² and the associated rejection
  sampler — J. Heinrich, *A Guide to the Pearson Type IV Distribution*,
  University of Pennsylvania, CDF/MEMO/STATISTICS/PUBLIC/6820 (2004).

* **The "independent generator" construction** — drawing independent univariate
  variates whose moments are solved so that a fixed linear mixing reproduces a
  target multivariate covariance, skewness and kurtosis — following the approach
  of C. D. Vale & V. A. Maurelli, "Simulating multivariate nonnormal
  distributions", *Psychometrika* 48 (1983).

The implementation was written to reproduce, bit for bit, the numerical output of
an earlier internal prototype used to calibrate this simulator, so that historical
results remain comparable. Reproducing identical numerical output from the same
published algorithm does not, in itself, make one implementation a copy of another.
